IMPORT prelude

-- Part I of the Interpretation Act 1978 (Northern Territory): Preliminary, sections 1 to 4.
-- Reprint as in force at 21 April 2023.
--
-- Section 1 (short title) and the repeals of section 2(1) and (2) are in the coverage table of NOTES.md;
-- the repeals are encoded in nt-schedule.l4 beside the Schedule they point at.
-- Each function answers JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE where the text itself says yes or no,
-- and NOTHING where the text does not say.

§ `Section 2: savings of earlier law`

-- The earlier law keeps working for a word, expression or provision in an Act (or a South Australian law applied to the Territory) made before this Act,
-- but only where this Act has no appropriate provision and an earlier law would have continued to be appropriate.
-- src:155 | (3) Where there is, in an Act, or a law of the State of South Australia in its application to the Northern Territory, made before the commencement of this Act, a word, expression or provision as to which there is no provision in this Act which is appropriate to its interpretation, application or effect but as to which a provision of a law in force before the commencement of this Act would, but for the repeal effected by this section, have continued to be appropriate to its interpretation, application or effect, the provision in that last-mentioned law continues to apply to the word, expression or provision in that first-mentioned law, notwithstanding the repeal effected by this section.
@ref s 2(3) (src:155)
GIVEN `the word, expression or provision is in an Act, or in a law of the State of South Australia in its application to the Northern Territory, made before the commencement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this Act has no provision that is appropriate to its interpretation, application or effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision of a law in force before the commencement would, but for the repeal effected by section 2, have continued to be appropriate to its interpretation, application or effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(3): the provision of the earlier law continues to apply to the word, expression or provision` MEANS
    JUST (`the word, expression or provision is in an Act, or in a law of the State of South Australia in its application to the Northern Territory, made before the commencement of this Act`
          AND `this Act has no provision that is appropriate to its interpretation, application or effect`
          AND `a provision of a law in force before the commencement would, but for the repeal effected by section 2, have continued to be appropriate to its interpretation, application or effect`)

-- For anything done or suffered before this Act commenced, the law in force when it was done is looked to, and not this Act.
-- src:156 | (4) Notwithstanding the repeal effected by this section, in the interpretation, application or effect of a word, expression or provision in an Act, or law of the State of South Australia in its application to the Northern Territory, to or in relation to anything done or suffered before the commencement of this Act, reference shall be made to the law as in force or deemed before the commencement of this Act to be in force at the time when that thing was done or suffered and not to this Act, and that law continues to have effect for that purpose.
@ref s 2(4) (src:156)
GIVEN `the word, expression or provision is in an Act, or in a law of the State of South Australia in its application to the Northern Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question is the interpretation, application or effect in relation to anything done or suffered before the commencement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(4): reference is made to the law in force when the thing was done or suffered, and not to this Act` MEANS
    IF   `the word, expression or provision is in an Act, or in a law of the State of South Australia in its application to the Northern Territory`
         AND `the question is the interpretation, application or effect in relation to anything done or suffered before the commencement of this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 3: application of this Act`

DECLARE `Kind of law in section 3(1)` IS ONE OF
    `an Act of the Legislative Assembly`
    `an Ordinance of the Northern Territory`
    `an Ordinance of the State of South Australia in its application to the Northern Territory`
    `an Act of the State of South Australia in its application to the Northern Territory`
    `a law of some other kind`

-- This Act applies to each Act, and to each Ordinance and each South Australian Act or Ordinance as applied to the Territory, as though that law were an Act.
-- The rule is "subject to section 2": where section 2 gives the earlier law effect, this Act does not apply.
-- Whether the law was made before or after this Act does not matter.
-- src:158 | (1) Subject to section 2, this Act applies to each Act, and to each Ordinance and Act of the State of South Australia in its application to the Northern Territory, and to each Ordinance of the Northern Territory, whether made before or after the making of this Act, including this Act, as though that law were an Act.
@ref s 3(1) (src:158)
GIVEN law IS A `Kind of law in section 3(1)`
      `section 2 gives the earlier law effect in the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1): this Act applies to the law as though the law were an Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER law
    WHEN `a law of some other kind` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST (NOT `section 2 gives the earlier law effect in the case`)

DECLARE `Capacity of the Crown` IS ONE OF
    `the Crown in right of the Territory`
    `the Crown in some other capacity`

-- This Act binds the Crown in right of the Territory, and the Crown in all its other capacities so far as the legislative power of the Legislative Assembly permits.
-- src:159 | (2) This Act binds the Crown not only in right of the Territory but, so far as the legislative power of the Legislative Assembly permits, the Crown in all its other capacities.
@ref s 3(2) (src:159)
GIVEN capacity IS A `Capacity of the Crown`
      `the legislative power of the Legislative Assembly permits it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(2): this Act binds the Crown in the capacity` MEANS
    CONSIDER capacity
    WHEN `the Crown in right of the Territory` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the Crown in some other capacity` THEN
        IF   `the legislative power of the Legislative Assembly permits it`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING

-- A provision of this Act yields to the appearance of an intention to the contrary in the provision it is applied to.
-- Without such an appearance the text does not say that the provision yields.
-- src:160 | (3) In the application of a provision of this Act to a provision, whether in this Act or in another law, the first-mentioned provision yields to the appearance of an intention to the contrary in that other provision.
@ref s 3(3) (src:160)
GIVEN `an intention to the contrary appears in the other provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(3): the provision of this Act yields to the other provision` MEANS
    IF   `an intention to the contrary appears in the other provision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 4: statutory instruments`

DECLARE `Thing to which section 4 may apply this Act` IS ONE OF
    `a statutory instrument made under a law to which this Act applies`
    `the interpretation, application and effect of such an instrument`
    `a reference to a statutory instrument`
    `a reference to an Act`
    `a thing of some other kind`

DECLARE `How section 4 applies this Act` IS ONE OF
    `as if the instrument were an Act`
    `as if the reference to the instrument were a reference to an Act`
    `as if the reference to an Act were a reference to such an instrument`

-- This Act applies, so far as it is applicable, to statutory instruments as if they were Acts, to references to instruments as if they were references to Acts, and to references to Acts as if they were references to such instruments.
-- src:162 | This Act applies, so far as it is applicable:
-- src:163 | (a) to and in respect of statutory instruments made under laws to which this Act applies, and to and in respect of the interpretation, application and effect of such instruments, as if those instruments were Acts; and
-- src:164 | (b) without limiting its general application:
-- src:165 | (i) to and in respect of references to statutory instruments as if they were references to Acts; and
-- src:166 | (ii) to and in respect of references to Acts as if they were references to such instruments.
@ref s 4 (src:162-166)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing to which section 4 may apply this Act`
      `this Act is applicable to the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `How section 4 applies this Act`
`s 4: the way in which this Act applies to the thing` MEANS
    IF   (NOT `this Act is applicable to the thing`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER thing
         WHEN `a statutory instrument made under a law to which this Act applies` THEN JUST `as if the instrument were an Act`
         WHEN `the interpretation, application and effect of such an instrument` THEN JUST `as if the instrument were an Act`
         WHEN `a reference to a statutory instrument` THEN JUST `as if the reference to the instrument were a reference to an Act`
         WHEN `a reference to an Act` THEN JUST `as if the reference to an Act were a reference to such an instrument`
         WHEN `a thing of some other kind` THEN NOTHING
